 "decisions": [
  {
   "id": "D-049",
   "text": "The generated streaming functions are preceded by `__attribute__((always_inline))`. The scope of the rule (these functions only, or every generated helper through one macro of the portability heade..."
  },
  {
   "id": "D-045",
   "text": "A test that crashes the Intel CPU runtime is not moved to a GPU; the cause is found first"
  },
  {
   "id": "D-044",
   "text": "`SetContext` carries `const BlockGeometry& block`"
  },
  {
   "id": "D-043",
   "text": "M0-8 is merged after its review fixes although tests 4, 6 and 7 are compiled out until M0-7b/7c; it counts as accepted only when they have run and I have viewed the box contour plot; TRACE rows say..."
  },
  {
   "id": "D-042",
   "text": "The 30-step box oracle of M0-8 uses force (1e-3, -2e-4, 0), tolerance 1e-6 unchanged"
  },
  {
   "id": "D-039",
   "text": "The portability header of ARCH-6 is emitted as two adjacent blocks at the top of every program: the backend prologue (qualifiers, `FMA`, contraction pragma) and the storage block of the accessor ge..."
  },
  {
   "id": "D-038",
   "text": "Backend after review of M0-1: devices are identified by enumeration position; write maps keep contents (no invalidate flag); the cache file has a verified header and is written through a per-proces..."
  },
  {
   "id": "D-037",
   "text": "Cell-type layout is canonical (descending width, then name); wall-like and not-updated kinds are declared in the manifest of the module that owns the group, not hard-coded in the registry"
  }
 ],
 "findings": [
  {
   "id": "IMPL-M0-26",
   "text": "no format for the schedule record; no place in the program for the tag, init and view kernels; VAL-7 names no generator or seeds and fixes TRT, whi... Fix: provisional record in brief M0-9 (confirmed by the M1-2 design note); kernels appended by a tail hook after the fused kernels; fixed seeds, SRT at..."
  },
  {
   "id": "IMPL-M0-25",
   "text": "`range` was checked for manifest defaults only; a configured value outside it reached the kernel Fix: configured values are checked against `range` and `range_open`"
  },
  {
   "id": "IMPL-M0-24",
   "text": "the order of the density and momentum sums was not stated, although bit comparisons with a host evaluation depend on it Fix: order stated"
  },
  {
   "id": "IMPL-M0-23",
   "text": "CORE-10 puts the uniform force first; the group order of ARCH-12 would run it last if another force fragment carried a set Fix: force fragments carry no set, order by `after`"
  },
  {
   "id": "IMPL-M0-22",
   "text": "CORE-7 refuses a viscosity of zero, but the inclusive `range` of `omega` in A.2 lets 2.0 through Fix: key `range_open`"
  },
  {
   "id": "IMPL-M0-21",
   "text": "parameter values were checked only when folded; a split axis with halo width 0 let a neighbour index leave the block; the brief gave the field writ... Fix: values checked always; neighbour access across a split axis without halo is refused; field write also in `moments-only`"
  },
  {
   "id": "IMPL-M0-20",
   "text": "which locals of which set a fragment may touch; \"readable after its first writer stage\" allowed reads of locals nobody wrote (`rho_w`, `omega`) and... Fix: scope rule per set; readable means written by a placed fragment or initialised by the assembler; `u` from stage 6; group order is fixed and a contr..."
  },
  {
   "id": "IMPL-M0-19",
   "text": "points the design notes left open for the streaming generator and the core modules: tag and init kernels have no slot in the generator interface; i... Fix: accepted as proposed in the briefs; the driver (M0-9) wires the tag and init kernels"
  }
 ]
}